The PAL suite's side-by-side test on witos (plan step R7.1): two libraries each link their own PAL, and the second
exports only its two entry points through a version script on Linux, FreeBSD and NetBSD. Without it on witos the second
library exported every PAL function, its calls bound to the first library's PAL, and a hardware exception in its PAL_TRY
was thrown by the other PAL as a type its catch did not match. witos takes the version script beside the other
platforms.

